Definition of Done

Settings is complete when:

all four pages visually belong to the same design system
the result is recognizably close to the supplied mockups
stock GNOME visual elements have not leaked into places where custom Bootcade visuals are required
existing Settings functionality is preserved
offline-only users remain first-class users
NET / ACCOUNT / HISCORES remain independent
Emulator architecture can accommodate future emulators
no fake functionality/data has been introduced just because it appears in a mockup
all four pages have been runtime-tested and captured

The mockups are the visual specification. Existing Bootcade behavior is the functional specification. Preserve the latter while replacing the former.